This function recursively traverses the schema and replaces `$ref` values.
If a user has a field named `$ref` in their model, it will be part of the schema.
Wait, if the user has a field named `$ref`, it will be in the `properties` of the schema.

Example:
```json
{
  "type": "object",
  "properties": {
    "$ref": { "type": "string" }
  }
}
```

In `_replace_refs`, it iterates over the keys of the schema.
If it encounters a key `$ref`, it assumes it's a JSON Schema reference and tries to replace it.

```python
